PasswordEncoder

Never store passwords in plain text.

Wrong:

Password@123

Correct:

$2a$10$Qfd...

Configuration:

@Bean
public PasswordEncoder passwordEncoder() {

    return new BCryptPasswordEncoder();
}


Why BCrypt?

Because BCrypt automatically:

Password

↓

Generate Salt

↓

Hash

↓

Store

Even if two users have the same password:

Password@123

Their hashes are different because each hash uses a unique salt.